 I think, that Mages (Wizards, Sorceres, whatever) give some part of
themselves to the mysterious forces they serve. Usually it's their 
body. Also, when they spend their long hours studying the books of
old, the Warriors train themselves for combat outdoors. It's clear
that their skills in weapons aren't good. Think yourself as a mage.
If you would somehow "mystically teleported" to a fantasy world, you
would propably be sorcerer in the eyes of the people in that world,
because of your great knowledge. 
 Then, imagine yourself in a combat - swinging a two-handed sword.
It would be hard for you to swing it, propably. The heaviests weight
about 20 pounds. But that's nothing. Wear a full plate armor, and you
aren't able to move at all. They weight about 70 pounds at least.
It would be easy to someone to dock from your weak swings, even if
you would be able to make them. Especially for someone trained in
combat for years.
 See what I mean. Of course, a Mage can become a warrior of some kind,
(like in the game of Moria) when you train yourself and gain physi-
cal skills by magical means. But you would always be a weaker fighter
than a Warrior of any kind.

